course: dictionary
lesson: 15861
title: Unfortunate and unfortunately
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unfortunate means having bad luck, or causing a sad or bad result. «The unfortunate team lost every match this year» tells you the team had bad luck. The words around it, lost every match, are the clue.
explain: Unfortunately is the adverb. It often starts a sentence with bad news. «Unfortunately, the picnic was cancelled because of the rain.» Ask yourself: is this good news or bad news? If it is bad, unfortunately is a good clue.
explain: In formal speech, «It is unfortunate that …» is a polite way to say that something is a pity. «It is unfortunate that the library is closed today» means it is a shame, not that the library is bad.
fact: Unfortunate means having bad luck, or causing sad or bad results.
fact: «An unfortunate accident» is an accident that causes harm or trouble.
fact: «Unfortunately» starts a sentence with bad news, like «Unfortunately, the trip was cancelled.»
fact: «It is unfortunate that …» is a polite, formal way to say something is a pity.
fact: Old-fashioned use: «an unfortunate» can be a poor or unlucky person.
exercise: «The unfortunate passengers stood in the rain, waiting for the late bus.» What does unfortunate mean here? | Very fast and clever | Happy and dancing | *Having bad luck | Quiet and shy
exercise: «Unfortunately, the picnic was cancelled because of the rain.» What does unfortunately tell the reader? | *The news is bad | The news is very good | Everyone is smiling | The picnic was a big success
exercise: Which phrase means it is a pity that something happened? | It is lucky that the sun came out | It is funny that the cat is asleep | It is wonderful that you won | *It is unfortunate that the shop closed early
test: «The unfortunate accident hurt nobody, but the car was dented.» What does unfortunate mean? | *Causing trouble or a sad result | Very quick and clever | Happy and loud | Made of gold
test: «Unfortunately, Sam forgot his lunch again.» What does the word unfortunately show? | Sam is on holiday | Sam is hungry for cake | *Bad news is coming | Good news is coming
exam: «She made an unfortunate remark about his shoes, and he went red.» What does unfortunate mean here? | Made of wood | Very fast and clever | Sweet and kind | *Not suitable and a bit embarrassing
